From 53d2c405973340121dcf9492ecedd31e2ebcfe8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gargrohin <29701609+gargrohin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 04:37:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] GR00T_N17 loader: skip video packets the requested frames
 don't need

After decoding only a shard's frames, PyAV still decoded every packet up to the last
requested one. These AV1 videos have a keyframe every 2 frames and no frame
reordering, so decode only from the last keyframe before each requested frame.
The fast path is used only when every packet has a pts, pts increase in decode
order and the first packet is a keyframe, and its result is checked (each fed
packet yields one frame, mapped by pts); otherwise it decodes all packets in order
as before. Frames are identical (30 random videos x 4 index sets); for 10% subsets
decode CPU drops 66 -> 16 ms per video.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
